{# ============================================================================
   THE OBSERVATION KINDS A RANGER PICKS FROM — the design's kinds.html, ported.

   IT IS A SECTION OF THE CONFIGURE PAGE that kept an address of its own, so it
   wears the configure page's heading and the configure page's strip, and the
   Configure action stays lit on it. The shell draws all three; nothing here
   draws navigation, and there is no way back other than the strip, the lit
   Configure and the crumb.

   It rhymes with the incident module's own kinds screen and shares a stylesheet
   vocabulary, but patrol's is SHALLOW: labels only, no behaviour blocks, no
   colour, no money.

   ONE ROUTE, TWO DATA CONDITIONS on the same address:
     · POPULATED — the two-pane manager (_manager.html.twig): kinds on the left,
       the selected kind's sub-categories on the right.
     · EMPTY — the first-run start (_empty.html.twig): the ghost sketch of a
       list's shape and the "write the first kind" path.

   AREA SCOPE, said once at the top and true of every read and write below: this
   list is THIS area's own, and nothing here is shared with another area.
   ========================================================================== #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiPatrol/base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Patrols · observation kinds{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {# The taxonomy admin's own `tx-` vocabulary, by the bundle's own constant so
       the path is never typed twice. Loaded only on this screen. #}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset(constant('Uhifadhi\\Patrol\\UhifadhiPatrolBundle::TAXONOMY_STYLESHEET')) }}">
{% endblock %}

{% block patrol_trail_tail %} <a href="{{ path('patrol_dashboard', {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">patrols</a> / kinds{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}{{ area.name }} — Patrols · configure{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_subtitle %}Everything this module is set up with in <b>this area</b>, in one place: how its dashboard is composed, the words a ranger picks from, and the numbers the module runs on.{% endblock %}

{# NO WAY BACK IS DRAWN HERE. The section strip, the lit Configure action and the
   crumb are the three ways back, and there is no fourth. #}
{% block shell_page_actions %}
    {% if recordScreens %}
        <a class="cta" href="{{ path('patrol_log', {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">{{ ux_icon('patrol:pen-line') }}Log patrol</a>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block patrol_page %}
    {# Area scope, said once, plainly — the one fact that changes how the page is
       read: the list is this area's, and editing needs Configure on Observation
       kinds — the Permissions screens' words for `observation-kinds.configure`. #}
    <div class="tx-say">{{ ux_icon('patrol:shield', {width: 17, height: 17}) }}<div><b>These kinds are {{ area.name }}&rsquo;s own.</b>
        Each area keeps its own observation kinds, so a change here reaches only the handsets patrolling {{ area.name }}.
        Editing needs <b>Configure</b> on <b>Observation kinds</b> — the authority over the words everybody else must
        use. Being able to log a patrol (<b>Record</b> on <b>Patrols</b>) is not enough.</div></div>

    {% if kinds is empty %}
        {{ include('@UhifadhiPatrol/kinds/_empty.html.twig') }}
    {% else %}
        {{ include('@UhifadhiPatrol/kinds/_manager.html.twig') }}
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}
